621716b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/mervinpraison-praisonai-50b53621716b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"mervinpraison/praisonai","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac5600a4c1684f809574df0aeb26430e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c0c6fa241303cc5730cafd03f5423522d821313b173d4fac6bb3131cc9b838e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework is framed as a five-layer stack (prompt, context, harness, loop, graph) plus a managed layer deciding where the agent runs, with each layer wrapping the one inside."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0d67bfe9ac7af15639aedb57120150e81a03a41c0f21ee6a3c6e520b941f92e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The core Python SDK exposes an Agent class constructed with parameters like instructions, role, goal, and output, and started via agent.start(...)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5257b89cd44710650b619e7f2e0830cd35aa49f7573c4d885bb5e6e4352f128f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Distribution is split into a core SDK (pip install praisonaiagents), a CLI package (pip install praisonai), optional extras for claw, flow, and ui, and an npm package named praisonai."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6026a1114b459f592abc0b17eb768f9e2271d75799f991f52830f5b0591da263"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents support an approval=True option described as a human gate before risky tools run, alongside guardrails and hooks in the harness layer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77465c804367522c8b66964e7a27fe7d080893a3d6f216df1012e4750e80620a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AgentFlow composes multi-step graphs with route(), parallel(), and repeat() steps, and the same graph can be expressed in YAML without Python."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9b035dfcd9c4e8efe879df445e4c7f55598bcaa6cfb1f8019b0b976603d70b89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom tools are defined with an @tool decorator on plain Python functions whose docstrings describe usage to the model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d418cdc7c4c65e2593b9f4c968b8cba197e24d918117c981a2193312f90869e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conversation state can be persisted to databases by passing a db() object with a database_url and session_id in the memory config, with messages, runs, and traces auto-persisted."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a52eae588fa7fd2c1606a8a8d4d4a65057dc1e9fdba32976f5dd86b230d97cc0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A whole agent (model calls, loop, and tools) can be placed on a managed runtime via run_on, e.g. run_on=\"anthropic\" hosted or run_on=\"docker\" self-hosted; invalid targets raise a TypeError."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d4ed013b3ee1954ed979bde78b4afb0dbebdff6c70ed0ea5aeb83556d79f7392"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The praisonai CLI offers subcommands for workflows, memory, knowledge, sessions, tools, MCP, scheduling, and managed sandboxes such as 'managed ps' and 'managed stop --all'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d8a7b329bbd820169566b5ced2372733cf6a5c0730cd6dc20d944a8b44acd6fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents accept memory, knowledge, and context parameters for persistence, selective retrieval, and auto-compaction, and handoffs isolate sub-agents to recent messages plus intersecting tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da0fe3e18e76737aabb7a4360f6da53c48a6dddb83d98c4b43058eb7b7173f73"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP servers are attached as tools via MCP(), supporting stdio commands, HTTP URLs, and WebSocket endpoints with auth tokens and environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e80065a90d4718f5fcec188c5a94a9f3c5b16da5b398ea34e8367ff0ee743544"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tool execution can be offloaded to shared sandboxes via tools_run_on with backends including docker, e2b, modal, daytona, flyio, and others, so steps in a flow share one sandbox filesystem."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c0c6fa241303cc5730cafd03f5423522d821313b173d4fac6bb3131cc9b838e","clm_0d67bfe9ac7af15639aedb57120150e81a03a41c0f21ee6a3c6e520b941f92e7","clm_5257b89cd44710650b619e7f2e0830cd35aa49f7573c4d885bb5e6e4352f128f","clm_6026a1114b459f592abc0b17eb768f9e2271d75799f991f52830f5b0591da263","clm_77465c804367522c8b66964e7a27fe7d080893a3d6f216df1012e4750e80620a","clm_9b035dfcd9c4e8efe879df445e4c7f55598bcaa6cfb1f8019b0b976603d70b89","clm_9d418cdc7c4c65e2593b9f4c968b8cba197e24d918117c981a2193312f90869e","clm_a52eae588fa7fd2c1606a8a8d4d4a65057dc1e9fdba32976f5dd86b230d97cc0","clm_d4ed013b3ee1954ed979bde78b4afb0dbebdff6c70ed0ea5aeb83556d79f7392","clm_d8a7b329bbd820169566b5ced2372733cf6a5c0730cd6dc20d944a8b44acd6fa","clm_da0fe3e18e76737aabb7a4360f6da53c48a6dddb83d98c4b43058eb7b7173f73","clm_e80065a90d4718f5fcec188c5a94a9f3c5b16da5b398ea34e8367ff0ee743544"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac5600a4c1684f809574df0aeb26430e","id":"pg_f8ec9585d33656b0a4f3d1e2739aee11","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mervinpraison-praisonai-readme-md-43a106db26d3-d1e2739aee11.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9d8940d0cfd752b3be1362afc603db8b"],"title":"MervinPraison/PraisonAI/README.md @ 43a106db26d3","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac5600a4c1684f809574df0aeb26430e"}
